{"toolCallId":"call_88fa13c5176b4a2cbb60f92a6cbdf44d","title":"Ran node, echo","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --apply; echo \"EXIT=$?\"","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --apply; echo \"EXIT=$?\"","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timeoutMs":120000,"cognition.ai/commandNames":["node","echo"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_9d80495b24394232a6281cc4024dff0e","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\n  - \"min percent flag task breakdown\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser and the exit point to confirm where the gate belongs (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T002 Read the existing Vitest cases to reuse their temporary-folder helper (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the script's Bash 3.2 constraints against the comparison style already used in the file (calculate-completeness.sh)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add the `MIN_PERCENT` global with an empty default so an absent option means no gate (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent` case to the argument parser, consuming the value with `shift 2` (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T006 Validate the value as an integer from 0 through 100 and exit 1 with an `ERROR:` line on stderr for a missing, non-numeric or out-of-range value (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T007 Replace the final `exit 0` with the threshold comparison: exit 3 when `MIN_PERCENT` is set and the reported percentage is below it, exit 0 otherwise (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T008 Read the per-file percentage in `--file` mode for the comparison, since that mode has no `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T009 Add the option, its 0-100 range and the exit-3 meaning to `show_help` and to the header usage comment (calculate-completeness.sh)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Add cases for below-floor, at-floor and `--min-percent 0` runs (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T011 Add cases for the three rejected inputs, asserting exit 1, an `ERROR:` line on stderr and no report on stdout (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T012 Add a stdout parity case that diffs a text run and a `--json` run with and without the option (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T013 Run the Vitest file and confirm the two pre-existing cases still pass (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T014 Run `validate.sh --strict` on this packet and record the RESULT line (specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\n  - \"min percent flag task breakdown\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser and the exit point to confirm where the gate belongs (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T002 Read the existing Vitest cases to reuse their temporary-folder helper (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the script's Bash 3.2 constraints against the comparison style already used in the file (calculate-completeness.sh)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add the `MIN_PERCENT` global with an empty default so an absent option means no gate (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent` case to the argument parser, consuming the value with `shift 2` (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T006 Validate the value as an integer from 0 through 100 and exit 1 with an `ERROR:` line on stderr for a missing, non-numeric or out-of-range value (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T007 Replace the final `exit 0` with the threshold comparison: exit 3 when `MIN_PERCENT` is set and the reported percentage is below it, exit 0 otherwise (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T008 Read the per-file percentage in `--file` mode for the comparison, since that mode has no `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T009 Add the option, its 0-100 range and the exit-3 meaning to `show_help` and to the header usage comment (calculate-completeness.sh)\n- [ ] T015 Emit a boolean `min_percent_met` field in the `--json` report when `--min-percent` is set, true at or above the floor and false below (REQ-009) (calculate-completeness.sh)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Add cases for below-floor, at-floor and `--min-percent 0` runs (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T011 Add cases for the three rejected inputs, asserting exit 1, an `ERROR:` line on stderr and no report on stdout (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T012 Add a stdout parity case that diffs a text run and a `--json` run with and without the option (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T013 Run the Vitest file and confirm the two pre-existing cases still pass (tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts)\n- [ ] T014 Run `validate.sh --strict` on this packet and record the RESULT line (specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
